  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local Experts Review FoodSafetyPlan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam has difficulties in assuring the safety of its food chain. A national food safety control system is lacking. The Vietnamese government is willing to improve the situation. The Vietnamese government recognize the Netherlands&#x2019; expertise in implementing food safety management systems. The Wageningen Food And Safety Research (WFSR) is developing, with the Vietnamese government, a plan to improve and strengthen the governmental reference laboratory structure, which will enable the Vietnamese food safety authority to execute its supervising duties according to international standards (MAT17VN02). In the present project, local experts will develop an additional but essential element for the WFSR project to develop a set of criteria for an international standard reference laboratory to assess and select an unlimited number of public laboratories, set up a plan to upgrade selected laboratories to join national reference laboratory network.</narrative>
  </description>
